# Site workflows (private template)

Copy this file to `site-workflows.local.md` in the same folder and adapt it.
`*.local.md` is gitignored, so machine- and site-specific conventions stay out
of the repository. Read the private copy, when it exists, before handling a
shorthand request.

Do not record patient names, IDs, accession numbers, or study UIDs here. Use
placeholders such as `<patient>` and `<date>`.

## Source nodes

Real hosts, ports, and AE titles belong in `examples/dicom_nodes.local.yaml`.
List only the node keys and their role here:

- `primary`: default source for same-day exams
- `secondary`: fallback / long-term archive

## Request shorthand used at this site

| The user says | Meaning at this site |
|---|---|
| "send me the exam of <patient>" | find today's study, verify the exact patient, C-GET, ZIP, upload to `<destination>`, reply with the link |
| "video of <patient>" | same lookup, then export the relevant series to MP4 and attach it |

## Delivery destinations

- Default upload destination: `<drive folder or rclone remote path>`
- Upload tool available to the agent: `<tool name>`
- Chat attachment convention: `<how this client expects files to be attached>`

## Same-day exam to MP4

1. C-ECHO `primary`, then study-level C-FIND by patient-name wildcard and
   today's `StudyDate`; verify the exact registered name.
2. C-GET the study into a per-request temporary folder.
3. `dicom_volume_video.py --path <folder> --out <videos> --list-series --include-descriptions --summary`
4. Export the clinically relevant series by `--series-number`.
5. Deliver the MP4, then clean the temporary download folder.

## Same-day exam to cloud drive

Follow `study-delivery-workflow.md` with the destination above.

## Local conventions

- Temporary/audit root: `<path>`
- Anything this site forbids or requires (for example, anonymize before any
  external share): `<notes>`
